<servinfo servinfosgmlid = "AENLSB0A1626020" svcinfotypenbr = "08" svcinfoqualnbr = "03" page = "2" supplyoff = "1" modify = "0">
<title>
Water Pump Drive Belt Inspection
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check water pump drive belt (1) for wear, cracks, deformation and contamination. If any defect is found, replace the belt with new one. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1626019"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Start engine and stop it after 2 or 3 seconds to stabilize water pump drive belt tension.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Hoist vehicle and remove right side front wheel. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A2406001"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove right side engine under side cover.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check water pump drive belt tension by tension meter following the instructions mentioned in the tension meter manual. If water pump drive belt tension is not as specified, replace the belt with new one.
</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>
Water pump drive belt tension
</title>
<ptxt>
Standard: 98 – 556 N (10.0 – 56.7 kgf or 22.0 – 125.0 lbf)
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Limit: 90 N (9.2 kgf or 20.2 lbf)
</ptxt>
</spec>
<spec>
<title>
Recommended belt tension meter specification
</title>
<ptxt>
Gates Corporation “508” or equivalent
</ptxt>
